<title>BRAZIL: French firm to buy control of Arno.</title>
<headline>French firm to buy control of Arno.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-03-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Sao Paulo Stock Exchange (Bovespa) said trade in Brazilian electrical appliance maker Arno has been suspended due to an agreement for the sale of a controlling interest to a French company.</p>
<p>The exchange said trade in the stock was suspended late Thursday following a request from the company, which has struck a deal to sell a controlling stake to French domestic appliance maker SEB.</p>
<p>In a published statement on Friday, Arno said its majority shareholders, which own 93.31 percent of Arno's voting shares, agreed to sell their stake to Groupe SEB for $162.3 million by April 30.</p>
<p>The bolsa said Arno stock would remain suspended Friday.</p>
<p>((--Fatima Cristina, Sao Paulo Newsroom, 5511 2485412))</p>
